// PARAM: --analysis interval
// Rejection case. A decimal constant larger than int64's maximum has no type
// under C 6.4.4.1p5's ladder -- the ladder runs out -- so it is a constraint
// violation rather than a value that wraps. The diagnostic names the literal
// and the bound instead of letting it silently become something else.
//
// This is also why int64's minimum cannot be written as a bare literal: the
// magnitude passes the bound before the negation applies. C has the same
// wart.
void main() {
  int64 x;
  x := 9223372036854775808
}
